<header><p class="st-kicker">khanate · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Khanate of Sibir</h1><p class="st-meta">1468 CE – 1598 CE (approx.) · capital Qashliq</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Tatar khanate of western Siberia whose defeat by Yermak's Cossacks in 1582 began Russia's conquest of Siberia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The khanate emerged from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tyumen-khanate">Tyumen Khanate</a> when the local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taibugids">Taibugid dynasty</a> seized power around 1495 and moved the capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qashliq">Qashliq</a> (Isker) on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irtysh">Irtysh</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaybanids">Shibanid</a> descendants of Jochi later contested the throne with the Taibugids.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Sibir ruled Siberian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatars</a> and tribute-paying forest peoples such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khanty">Khanty</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mansi">Mansi</a>, whose fur tribute was its main wealth. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taibugids">Taibugid</a> ruler Yadegar paid tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV</a> from 1555, but in 1563 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaybanids">Shibanid</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuchum">Kuchum</a> seized power, stopped payments and promoted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> among his subjects with missionaries from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1582 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yermak-timofeyevich">Yermak</a>, employed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stroganov-family">Stroganov</a> merchants, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qashliq">Qashliq</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuchum">Kuchum</a> fought on from the steppe until his final defeat on the Ob in 1598, after which the khanate's lands became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/khanate-of-sibir.jpg" alt="Khanate of Sibir" width="320" height="265"><figcaption>Image: Başqurd · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sibirkhanligi.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1468 CE – 1598 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>khanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Qashliq</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Yadegar, Kuchum</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Siberian Tatar</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Siberian Khanate, Sibir Khanate</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1533&amp;focus=khanate-of-sibir" aria-label="Khanate of Sibir on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6119 231 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Khanate of Sibir lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6439 487L6409 496M6439 487L5820 533"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6409 496h0M5820 533h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6439 487h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6439 487h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1533&amp;focus=khanate-of-sibir">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
